I wrote both briefs for issue #104 and the harness accepted them, so they're now fixed. I changed nothing in the repository.

**Builder brief.** It asks for one PR that rewrites only `packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js` and leaves `packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js` as it is. The new CLI:
- checks every file named, in order;
- reads `-` from stdin and reports it as `-`;
- rejects a second `-` as a usage error with exit 2, before reading anything;
- on a file it can't read, writes the error to stderr and goes on to the next file.

The builder also adds `node:test` cases for every situation the issue lists, updates the package README, and makes sure the PR body says "Closes …/issues/104". It then waits for the test workflow to pass.

**Verifier brief.** It has six checks, one per acceptance line, in the same order. Each one runs the CLI against small sample files, `git diff`, the test suite or `gh` commands, and says what counts as PASS and what counts as FAIL. A few extra checks are listed under an Advisory heading and don't affect the result.

**One rule I settled myself:** the issue doesn't say which exit code wins when one file can't be read and another has bad rows. I told the builder that exit 2 wins over exit 1, since the issue gives exit 2 whenever "any file can't be read". The verifier only checks this under Advisory, so it can't fail the PR.
